{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-fe59a081-e2a6-463a-adb9-f4ce8e72f37d","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-87606496381cc47e","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-9016-4b1a_j4m/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-9016-E001.md","content":"# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n\n## Description\n\nCluster administrators get per-project reporting of idle and stale resources directly in\nthe RHOAI web console: an idle-workbench report showing each workbench's last activity,\nowner, and reserved resources, and a stale pipeline-run report showing completed runs\nolder than a configurable age together with their retained artifacts. Either report can\nbe exported as CSV so administrators can act on the data outside the console. The reports\nare read-only — they give administrators the confidence to reclaim capacity manually;\nautomated reclamation and cost/chargeback calculations remain out of scope.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Idle-workbench report, shown per project: for each workbench, its last activity\n  (sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking), its owner, and its reserved\n  resources.\n- Stale pipeline-run report, shown per project: completed pipeline runs older than a\n  configurable age, with their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run\n  completion metadata.\n- An administrator-configurable age threshold for the stale pipeline-run report.\n- CSV export of either report, covering the columns the report displays.\n- Read-only reporting only: no reclamation or deletion actions are offered from the\n  reports (automated reclamation and cost/chargeback are out of scope for the strategy).\n- Validation of the two passive data sources as part of delivery: confirm that the\n  notebook controller's activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines' run-completion metadata\n  expose the fields the reports need, in a form the console can read.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- Given a project containing workbenches, when an administrator opens the idle-workbench\n  report, then each workbench is listed with its last activity, owner, and reserved\n  resources, populated from the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the\n  stale pipeline-run report, then the runs older than the configured age are listed with\n  their retained artifacts, populated from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n- Given an administrator changes the stale-run age threshold, then the stale pipeline-run\n  report reflects the new threshold.\n- Given either report is displayed, when the administrator exports it as CSV, then a CSV\n  containing the report's displayed columns is produced.\n- The reports are visible to administrators consistent with the console's existing\n  project-scoped RBAC.\n- Every report field is verified to populate from its stated source (notebook-controller\n  activity tracking for the workbench report; Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata for the\n  pipeline-run report) against live cluster data.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved\n  resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking — covered by this\n  epic.\n- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age\n  with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata — covered by this\n  epic.\n- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — bundled with the P1 report work\n  because it extends the same report surfaces and the same data-access plumbing; a\n  separate epic would double-touch the same UI and data-access code.\n\n## Risks / Notes\n\n- The strategy assumes the notebook controller's per-workbench last-activity data is\n  readable by the console. The architecture context confirms the tracking exists, but the\n  console consumes the Kubernetes API and its established component integrations; if the\n  last-activity timestamp is not exposed in a console-readable form, follow-up work in the\n  notebook controller (Notebooks component, Workbenches team) will be required and the\n  decomposition should be revisited.\n- The notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines are passive components in this strategy:\n  they keep working as-is, and their continued provision of the report data is validated\n  by this epic's acceptance criteria rather than by separate validation epics.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":45257,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-96a28f8864c19364","agent_id":"a282a50d93546ae84","session_id":"0862132f-9e49-42c1-8562-e738ee3eb185","uuid":"9632862a-93fb-442c-83ae-f88d38ad2667","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:08:10.239Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-9016"}
