{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4b5ab6ab97bf2da","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-9016-E001\n3\ttitle: Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-9016\n5\tcomponent: Dashboard\n6\tteam: RHOAI Dashboard\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P1\n9\tai_signals:\n10\t  change_specificity: 0\n11\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n12\t  adapter_pattern: 0\n13\t  existing_foundation: 1\n14\t  open_questions: 0\n15\t  external_dependency: 1\n16\t  human_process_gates: 1\n17\t  repo_access: 1\n18\t  architecture_claims: 1\n19\timplementation_type: null\n20\tdependencies: []\n21\tinvestigation_signals: null\n22\tai_implementability: High\n23\tai_implementability_score: 6\n24\tjira_key: null\n25\tbranch: null\n26\tgated_by: null\n27\tgate_failure_impact: null\n28\t---\n29\t# Idle and stale resource reports in the RHOAI web console\n30\t\n31\t## Description\n32\t\n33\tCluster administrators get per-project reporting of idle and stale resources directly in\n34\tthe RHOAI web console: an idle-workbench report showing each workbench's last activity,\n35\towner, and reserved resources, and a stale pipeline-run report showing completed runs\n36\tolder than a configurable age together with their retained artifacts. Either report can\n37\tbe exported as CSV so administrators can act on the data outside the console. The reports\n38\tare read-only — they give administrators the confidence to reclaim capacity manually;\n39\tautomated reclamation and cost/chargeback calculations remain out of scope.\n40\t\n41\t## Scope\n42\t\n43\t- Idle-workbench report, shown per project: for each workbench, its last activity\n44\t  (sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking), its owner, and its reserved\n45\t  resources.\n46\t- Stale pipeline-run report, shown per project: completed pipeline runs older than a\n47\t  configurable age, with their retained artifacts, sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run\n48\t  completion metadata.\n49\t- An administrator-configurable age threshold for the stale pipeline-run report.\n50\t- CSV export of either report, covering the columns the report displays.\n51\t- Read-only reporting only: no reclamation or deletion actions are offered from the\n52\t  reports (automated reclamation and cost/chargeback are out of scope for the strategy).\n53\t- Validation of the two passive data sources as part of delivery: confirm that the\n54\t  notebook controller's activity tracking and Kubeflow Pipelines' run-completion metadata\n55\t  expose the fields the reports need, in a form the console can read.\n56\t\n57\t## Acceptance Criteria\n58\t\n59\t- Given a project containing workbenches, when an administrator opens the idle-workbench\n60\t  report, then each workbench is listed with its last activity, owner, and reserved\n61\t  resources, populated from the notebook controller's activity tracking.\n62\t- Given a project containing completed pipeline runs, when an administrator opens the\n63\t  stale pipeline-run report, then the runs older than the configured age are listed with\n64\t  their retained artifacts, populated from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata.\n65\t- Given an administrator changes the stale-run age threshold, then the stale pipeline-run\n66\t  report reflects the new threshold.\n67\t- Given either report is displayed, when the administrator exports it as CSV, then a CSV\n68\t  containing the report's displayed columns is produced.\n69\t- The reports are visible to administrators consistent with the console's existing\n70\t  project-scoped RBAC.\n71\t- Every report field is verified to populate from its stated source (notebook-controller\n72\t  activity tracking for the workbench report; Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata for the\n73\t  pipeline-run report) against live cluster data.\n74\t\n75\t## HLR Traceability\n76\t\n77\t- HLR-1 (P1): per-project idle-workbench report (last activity, owner, reserved\n78\t  resources) sourced from the notebook controller's activity tracking — covered by this\n79\t  epic.\n80\t- HLR-2 (P1): stale pipeline-run report (completed runs older than a configurable age\n81\t  with retained artifacts) sourced from Kubeflow Pipelines run metadata — covered by this\n82\t  epic.\n83\t- HLR-3 (P2, bundled): CSV export of either report — bundled with the P1 report work\n84\t  because it extends the same report surfaces and the same data-access plumbing; a\n85\t  separate epic would double-touch the same UI and data-access code.\n86\t\n87\t## Risks / Notes\n88\t\n89\t- The strategy assumes the notebook controller's per-workbench last-activity data is\n90\t  readable by the console. The architecture context confirms the tracking exists, but the\n91\t  console consumes the Kubernetes API and its established component integrations; if the\n92\t  last-activity timestamp is not exposed in a console-readable form, follow-up work in the\n93\t  notebook controller (Notebooks component, Workbenches team) will be required and the\n94\t  decomposition should be revisited.\n95\t- The notebook controller and Kubeflow Pipelines are passive components in this strategy:\n96\t  they keep working as-is, and their continued provision of the report data is validated\n97\t  by this epic's acceptance criteria rather than by separate validation epics.\n98\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cb651cb9689d071","agent_id":"ac3ae05d520a9366a","session_id":"0862132f-9e49-42c1-8562-e738ee3eb185","uuid":"ebe6aded-5a5d-4c26-adbd-8e6aaf251886","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:09:43.116Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-b4b5ab6ab97bf2da","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
