n steps an administrator can take based on the reports (manual actions\n50\t  only — automated reclamation and cost/chargeback calculations are out of scope for the\n51\t  strategy), including the cautions that make reclamation safe.\n52\t\n53\t## Acceptance Criteria\n54\t\n55\t- Documentation topics explaining both reports (fields, data sources, interpretation) and\n56\t  CSV export are authored and delivered through the Red Hat docs content process.\n57\t- Safe manual reclamation steps are documented, consistent with the strategy's\n58\t  out-of-scope boundary on automated reclamation and cost/chargeback.\n59\t- The documentation is technically reviewed against the implemented reports by the\n60\t  console engineering team, and any inaccuracies found in review are corrected.\n61\t\n62\t## HLR Traceability\n63\t\n64\t- HLR-4 (P2): documentation explains the reports and safe reclamation steps — covered by\n65\t  this epic.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9cb651cb9689d071","agent_id":"ac3ae05d520a9366a","session_id":"0862132f-9e49-42c1-8562-e738ee3eb185","uuid":"b0ae11e5-7c95-498a-b4bf-0ca56c0cc676","timestamp":"2026-10-26T10:09:43.845Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8dfc280861d2eab7","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Review RHAISTRAT-9016 decomposition"}
